# Rules for Every AI Agent in this Workspace

Read this first before executing any tasks.

## 1. Who You Are Working With
- **User Role**: The user is the product owner / architect — the AI agents are the developers.
- **Communication Style**: Plain words, short answers, zero fluff or sycophancy.
- **Pacing**: One step at a time, then pause and wait for user confirmation.
- **Finished Work Report**:
  1. What changed
  2. Where it is located
  3. What is left to do
- **Attribution Rule**: Never write an AI's name in filenames, commit messages, author tags, or script headers.

## 2. Linear Continuity & Active Context
- Live system state: Always read `~/ACTIVE_CONTEXT.md` before proposing changes.
- It lists active task desks, master to-dos, and recent runs.
- Continue work linearly from where the previous agent left off — never re-invent or discard valid work without reason.

## 3. Multi-Agent Delegation & Awareness
Different agents have distinct capabilities. Cooperate and recommend hand-offs when appropriate:
- **Claude Code**: Complex software architecture, large refactors, full-stack systems, SVG design.
- **OpenAI Codex**: High-precision backend logic, algorithmic scripts, automated testing.
- **Google Gemini**: Massive context digestion, repo-wide audits, multi-document research.
- **Hermes Agent**: Autonomous system execution, background workflows, desktop tool-calling.
- **Devin**: End-to-end task solving, standalone project construction.
- **OpenCode**: Flexible terminal AI coding with multi-provider model routing.
- **Qwen Code**: High-efficiency coding, local model inference.
- **Kilo**: Rapid terminal workflows, GUI control applications.
- **Cursor IDE**: Visual multi-file code editing, in-editor diff review, live debugging.
- **OpenClaw**: Sandboxed VM execution for untrusted network scraping and bots.
- **Browser-Use**: Autonomous web navigation and form automation.
- **Cline & Aether**: Autonomous CLI coding agents.

## 4. Never
- Delete or overwrite files without inspecting them first.
- Push or force-push to main without approval.
- Expose secrets or API keys.
